---
description: Checklist for adding or extending Bling API modules
globs: src/entities/**,src/bling.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Extending Entity Modules

Use Bling's official reference as the source of truth: https://developer.bling.com.br/referencia

## New Resource Module

1. **Create folder** `src/entities/<camelCaseName>/` matching an existing naming pattern (`src/entities/depositos/`, `src/entities/gruposDeProdutos/`).

2. **Add `index.ts`** — class extending `Entity`, one method per Bling operation. Follow `src/entities/camposCustomizados/index.ts` for a medium module or `src/entities/empresas/index.ts` for a minimal one.

3. **Add interfaces** — one file per operation in `interfaces/` named `<operation>.interface.ts` (e.g. `find.interface.ts`, `post-stock.interface.ts`). Export `I<Operation>Params`, `I<Operation>Body`, `I<Operation>Response` as needed. See `src/entities/nfes/interfaces/`.

4. **Add types** — union/enum types in `types/<name>.type.ts` when Bling documents discrete values. See `src/entities/contatos/types/criterio.type.ts`, `src/entities/nfes/types/situacao.type.ts`.

5. **Reuse `@shared`** — import from `../../@shared/types/` (relative) only when the value set matches. Do not reuse shared `situacao.type.ts` for a different Bling situação enum.

6. **Register in facade** — import and add getter in `src/bling.ts`.

7. **Add tests** — `__tests__/index.spec.ts` plus `*-response.ts` fixtures. Mirror `src/entities/camposCustomizados/__tests__/`.

8. **Update README** — entity checklist in `README.md` if the resource is user-facing.

## New Operation on Existing Module

1. Add interface file under the module's `interfaces/`.
2. Add entity method calling the correct repository verb (see `architecture/repository-layer.mdc`).
3. Add fixture + spec case in `__tests__/`.
4. Match HTTP verb used by siblings for the same semantic (PATCH situation → `update` vs `replace`; check the resource's existing `changeSituation`).

## Choosing `update` vs `replace`

- Bling **PATCH** partial updates → `repository.update` (`src/entities/camposCustomizados/index.ts`).
- Bling **PUT** full resource replace → `repository.replace` (`src/entities/contatos/index.ts` `update` method).
- Verify against Bling docs; the repository maps both to HTTP PATCH in `src/repositories/bling.repository.ts`.

## Special Cases

- **Response headers required** — set `shouldIncludeHeadersInResponse: true` (`src/entities/homologacao/index.ts`). Homologação is the headers example, not GET-with-body.
- **GET with body** — `IIndexOptions` allows optional `body`; no current entity uses it. Add only if [Bling reference](https://developer.bling.com.br/referencia) documents a GET payload.
- **Non-CRUD action endpoints** — name the method after the Bling action; use `store` for POST actions (`src/entities/pedidosVendas/index.ts`).
- **Orchestration** — `Homologacao.execute()` sequences other entity methods and returns `Promise<void>`; ordinary CRUD methods `await this.repository.*` and use `Promise<null>` when Bling has no body.

## Do Not

- Create alternate HTTP clients outside `src/repositories/` (OAuth token/revoke HTTP belongs in `src/auth/oauth-client.ts` only).
- Put test fixtures in `interfaces/` or production types in `__tests__/`.
- Skip `@see` links to Bling reference in JSDoc.
